The graph shows a parabola $y = x^2$ with a secant through $(1, 1)$ and $(3, 9)$, and a tangent at $(2, 4)$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, scale=0.85]
\draw[->] (0,0) -- (4.5,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[->] (0,0) -- (0,5.5) node[above] {$y$};
\foreach \x in {1,2,3,4} {\draw (\x,0) -- (\x,-0.12); \node[below,font=\scriptsize] at (\x,-0.12) {$\x$};}
\foreach \y/\val in {1/2,2/4,3/6,4/8,5/10} {\draw (-0.12,\y) -- (0,\y); \node[left,font=\scriptsize] at (-0.12,\y) {$\val$};}
\node[below left,font=\scriptsize] at (0,0) {$0$};
\draw[thick,blue,domain=0:3.15,smooth,variable=\x] plot (\x, {0.5*\x*\x}) node[above left] {$y=x^2$};
\draw[thick,dashed,red] (0.75,0.0) -- (3.25,5.0) node[right] {secant};
\draw[thick,teal] (1.0,0.0) -- (3.0,4.0) node[right] {tangent};
\fill (2,2.0) circle (2.5pt) node[below right] {$(2,4)$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
Compare the gradient of the secant line across $[1, 3]$ with the gradient of the tangent at $x = 2$.

The graph of $y = f(x)$ has turning points at $x = -1$ and $x = 3$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}, scale=0.8]
\draw[->] (-3,0) -- (5,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[->] (0,-3) -- (0,4) node[above] {$y$};
\foreach \x in {-2,-1,1,2,3,4} {\draw (\x,0) -- (\x,-0.12); \node[below,font=\scriptsize] at (\x,-0.12) {$\x$};}
\node[below left,font=\scriptsize] at (0,0) {$0$};
\draw[thick,blue] plot[smooth,tension=0.6] coordinates {(-2.5,-1.5) (-1,2.5) (1,0) (3,-2) (4.5,2)} node[above right] {$y=f(x)$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
Identify the intervals of $x$ where $f'(x) > 0$ and where $f'(x) < 0$.

The graph shows tangents at four points $A, B, C, D$ along a curve.
